From e48b4e0fc2ad72e3108c45786be9fa6ce1ae1c38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp2@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:44:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mips: fix post-DMA cache flush on 1004K/34K without IOCU

EcoNet EN7528 (dual-core 1004Kc, 4 VPEs) and EN751221 (34Kc, up to 2
VPEs) have CONFIG_CPU_HAS_PREFETCH but no IOCU, so device DMA does not
snoop the L1/L2 caches. Linux only performs arch_sync_dma_for_cpu()
when cpu_needs_post_dma_flush() is true; 1004K/34K are not in that
list and do not implement MAAR, so dma_sync_single_for_cpu() is a
no-op.

On SMP a foreign core can speculatively fill a DMA buffer (page_pool
recycle, skb head, etc.) while the engine is still writing. The stale
line later writebacks over a kmem_cache object -- seen as:

  CPU n Unable to handle kernel paging request
  kmem_cache_alloc_noprof / inet_twsk_alloc
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt

after a Wi-Fi client joins and generates TCP TIME_WAIT churn. maxcpus=1
hides it by removing the other L1; it is not a driver regression.

Treat 1004K and 34K like BMIPS5000 for this check: neither has MAAR,
and once cpu_needs_post_dma_flush() is true the existing non-inclusive
r4k_dma_cache_inv() path already invalidates via bc_inv() (mips_sc_inv:
Hit_Writeback_Inv_SD on both edge lines plus a full range blast), so no
change is needed there.

Verified on hardware: TP-Link EX20v (EN7528, 4 VPEs online, no
maxcpus=1 workaround needed). Reproduced reliably with a 10-thread TCP
hammer against the router (586 concurrent TIME_WAIT sockets) both on
current HEAD and on an older known-good commit, ruling out a driver
regression; zero oops across repeated runs after this fix. EN751221
boards (e.g. TP-Link Archer C5v) ship single-threaded by default and
are unaffected until a second VPE is brought up, at which point the
same race applies; the CPU_34K arm covers that case.

Signed-off-by: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp2@gmail.com>
---
 arch/mips/mm/dma-noncoherent.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mm/dma-noncoherent.c b/arch/mips/mm/dma-noncoherent.c
index ab4f2a7..8c24174 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mm/dma-noncoherent.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/dma-noncoherent.c
@@ -33,6 +33,14 @@ static inline bool cpu_needs_post_dma_flush(void)
 	case CPU_BMIPS5000:
 	case CPU_LOONGSON2EF:
 	case CPU_XBURST:
+	/*
+	 * 1004Kc (EN7528) and 34Kc (EN751221) implement prefetch but
+	 * EcoNet parts have no IOCU, so DMA is not hardware-coherent.
+	 * Post-DMA invalidate is required on SMP or recycled buffers
+	 * write back into the slab allocator.
+	 */
+	case CPU_1004K:
+	case CPU_34K:
 		return true;
 	default:
 		/*
-- 
